-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Reused code or algorithmic structure
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

ML-MAWS (https://github.com/PapriSaha/ML-MAWS, commit
0c38db12d9ad271aafcb4940d7558dfcd00925c1)
  License: Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE.txt of the repository). The
  repository names no copyright holder in its license file and has no
  NOTICE file; the authors of the accompanying paper are P. Saha,
  S. K. Das, A. Sarkar and M. M. Hasan (arXiv:2606.25584).
  Reused: the algorithmic structure of MAW enumeration on a suffix
  automaton, the entropy-based selection of MAW lengths, the adaptive
  length range, and the construction and column capping of the binary
  matrix, reimplemented in Rust in crates/qmaws-core (maw.rs,
  matrix.rs). No ML-MAWS source code is included.

wQFM (https://github.com/Mahim1997/wQFM-2020, version 1.4, commit
7bfdf8e77bd9079c708c831f1fb8404cc6821809)
  License: Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE.md of the repository). The
  repository names no copyright holder in its license file and has no
  NOTICE file; the authors of the accompanying paper are M. Mahbub,
  Z. Wahab, R. Reaz, M. S. Rahman and M. S. Bayzid (Bioinformatics
  37:3734-3743, 2021, doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btab428).
  Reused: the wQFM algorithm as implemented in its Java code (greedy
  initial bipartition, the [s] - beta [v] partition score, the FM-style
  refinement with its tie-breaking and stopping rules, dummy taxa with
  mean-weighted merged quartets, and the merging of subtrees),
  reimplemented in Rust in crates/qmaws-core (amalgamate.rs) as wQFM-rs.
  No wQFM source code is included.

Reference trees and name tables in data/references/ were checked against
files of the ML-MAWS repository; see data/references/SOURCE.md.
